{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["And Elohim said: Let there be a rakia — after the first day had been completed at its morning, ויאמר אלהים." "Rakia — it is a noun of action, like עשיר whose interpretation is 'enriched,' חסיד — 'acted kindly.' Because from the earth to the upper heavens there were waters, as written: מרחפת על פני המים — now the Holy One, blessed be He, divided them in the middle, and made a flattened sheet spread out from east to west and from north to south, to separate between the upper waters. And because the work of the waters was not completed until the third day, when the dry land appeared, 'that it was good' is not said on the second day; but on the third day 'that it was good' is said twice — once for the work of the waters and once for the sprouting of the trees and the vegetation." "Between waters and waters — so that half of them are above and half below."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T23:16:44.689843179Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}